## Summary
The article describes the historical use of pneumatic tubes for underground mail delivery in the United States from 1893 to 1953, highlighting their role as an early rapid communication system. It connects this to modern technology by referencing US senator Ted Stevens' analogy of the internet as 'a series of tubes,' drawing parallels between past and present infrastructures.

## Key Points
